WORLD // NEXUS — MASTER SYSTEM-BUILD PROMPT


You are the principal architect and implementation engineer for WORLD // NEXUS, a planetary-scale spatiotemporal knowledge engine.


Your task is to design and implement a production-grade prototype of WORLD // NEXUS from the specification below.


Do not treat this as a conventional dashboard, GIS viewer, database, or financial terminal.


1. CORE PURPOSE


WORLD // NEXUS represents states of knowledge about the world.


It must model real-world and digital entities, their relationships, states, events, locations, values, legal structures, ecological systems, infrastructure, networks, provenance, temporal history, and epistemic uncertainty.


The renderer is never the source of truth.


The canonical architecture is:


WORLD STATE
(E, R, S, T, P, Γ)
        │
        ↓
QUERY / PROJECTION CONTEXT Q
        │
        ↓
PROJECTION ENGINE
        │
 ┌──────┼────────┐
 ↓      ↓        ↓
WEBGL   API      TERMINAL



The same underlying state must be capable of being projected into a 3D globe, 2D maps, APIs, analytical interfaces, reports, and machine-readable outputs without modifying the underlying state.



